:: OC Isaiah Snakes in the Grass [nobr]

/* Intro */
You notice <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Isaiah</span> and his friends hanging out at the their lunch table and decide to walk over and join them. Everyone greets you as usual, except strangely for <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Isaiah</span>. <span style="color:Yellow">He’s hunched over his untouched tray. His expression shows he’s disengaged from the table. You sit across from him without saying a word. He seems to notice you, but doesn’t offer his normal smile, so you ask him what’s up.</span> <br>

    <<set _ad to [
        {
            Name: "Player",
            State: {
                Mouth: "Frown",
            },
        },
        {
            Name: "OC Zay",
            State: {
                Outfit: "Uniform",
                Mouth: "Frown",
                Eyes: "Tired",
            },
        },
    ]>>
    <<ad _ad>>

<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Isaiah</span> lets out a sigh as he shrugs, eyeing his tray. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Mr. K</span> says we aren’t allowed to go into the music room during recess on Mondays, Wednesday, and Fridays anymore.”</span> He grumbles. You ask why he was banned on those days. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“He said something stupid about making it fair for everyone to enjoy the equipment in the room, which is ridiculous! I’m not stopping anyone from going in there. I just… show up and play! That’s it!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Isaiah</span> sighs again, picking up his sandwich and taking a slightly angry bite. <br>
<br>
You’re about to say something, but the boy sitting next to you interjects. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I bet it was <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span> and his crew. Maybe, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Zay</span>, we all should go over there and have a little chat with them bums?”</span> The boy asks, pointing at <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span>’s table. <br>
<br>
As everyone around you starts hyping up the idea, you glance over at <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Isaiah</span>. He notices you staring and lets out another sigh. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Guys… we’re not gonna crash out over a piano.”</span> He waves for everyone to relax. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Well, at least not right now.”</span> You raise an eyebrow and ask what he means by that and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Isaiah</span> locks eyes with you. <br>
<br>
But before he can speak, someone clears his throat <span style="color:Yellow">and you look up to see <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span> standing over <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Isaiah</span> with his smaller than usual crew behind him.</span> <br>

    <<set _ad to [
        {
            Name: "Player",
            State: {
                Mouth: "Frown",
                Blush: 1,
            },
        },
        {
            Name: "OC Zay",
            State: {
                Outfit: "Uniform",
                Mouth: "Frown",
                Eyes: "Mad",
            },
        },
        {
            Name: "Xavier",
            State: {
                Outfit: "Uniform",
                Mouth: "Smirk",
                Eyes: "Tired",
            },
        },
    ]>>
    <<ad _ad>>

<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Hello, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Isaiah</span>, just checking in on my musically inclined friend. You look so down, I almost thought you were going to cry into your sandwich.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span> chuckles, causing his posse to laugh beside him. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I heard the teacher isn’t letting you into the music room anymore. So sad that the music boy has been silenced.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span> tries to sound sincere, but it is obvious he is enjoying himself. <span style="color:Yellow">You look to <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Isaiah</span>, who doesn’t move. He stares straight ahead like <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span> isn’t even there.</span> <br>
<br>
You turn back to see <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span> walk around the table as <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jake</span> grins and leans closer to <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Isaiah</span>. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Well, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span>, I think it’s good that they shut this one up.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jake</span> chuckles as <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span> sits down next to you, <span style="color:Yellow">shoving you slightly so that he is across from <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span>.</span> <br>
<br>

<<linkreplace"Continue">>
    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Shut up, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jake</span>.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span> says, not harshly, but like a command. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jake</span> tenses up and silences himself. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“But you’re right. If only this one had fallen in line, he would have gotten whatever he wanted and more.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span> glances around the table, everyone has gone quiet. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Let me spell it out for you, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Isaiah</span>. This school works in a certain way. There is a line, so to speak. You are supposed to follow it. Not to stand out, not acting special, unless I want you to. You didn’t follow the line.”</span> Silence follows <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span>’s words; he lets them linger in the air like a miasma before he continues. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“So now?”</span> He leans forward, calm but stern, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Now I’m going to make your life here miserable until you learn to follow the line. And trust me, I’m very good at it.”</span> Another long pause as <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span>’s eyes flicker to the rest of the table. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Let’s go.”</span> <br>
    <br>
    <span style="color:LightCoral">Everyone at the table picks up their trays and leaves, not just <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span>’s goons but those who had backed up <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Isaiah</span> just a moment ago. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span>’s presence alone had made them abandon him and follow <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span> without hesitation out of fear, leaving just you and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Isaiah</span> at the table.</span> <br>

